# 🤖 Self-Improving Python Utilities

This repository demonstrates a fully automated, self-improving Python codebase using LLMs (Large Language Models) and ephemeral CI infrastructure.

- **Automated code improvement:** Every 2 hours, an LLM agent reviews and enhances the codebase, creating a Pull Request with improvements if all tests pass.
- **Ephemeral CI runners:** Tests are executed on temporary Hetzner VPS machines, which are created and destroyed automatically to minimize costs and maximize security.
- **Zero public SSH exposure:** All CI runners are accessible only via secure tunnels.

---

## 🚀 Features

### 1. LLM-Powered Self-Improvement

- The `improve_agent.py` script uses OpenAI GPT-4o to:
  - Add type hints and docstrings
  - Refactor and optimize code
  - Add new utility functions with corresponding tests
- Improvements are committed only if all tests pass.
- Automated workflow runs every 2 hours via GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/self-improve.yml`).

### 2. Ephemeral Hetzner CI Runners

- On each pull request or code change, a minimal Hetzner VPS is provisioned using [Cyclenerd/hcloud-github-runner](https://github.com/Cyclenerd/hcloud-github-runner).
- The runner is accessible only via secure tunnels (no public SSH).
- After tests complete, the VPS is deleted to avoid unnecessary costs (approx. €0.01 per test run).
- See `.github/workflows/deploy-runner.yml` for details.

